---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title={'Projects'} description={'Systems built by Phoenix I/O, including the MedTransport dispatch and crew platform and a sub-millisecond trading system.'} page="projects">
<section class="page" id="p-projects" data-title="Projects">
  <div class="pagehead"><div class="wrap"><span class="label">Projects</span><h1>Built by Phoenix I/O.</h1><p class="lede">For engagements our principals led at prior firms, see <a href="/past-performance/">Past Performance</a>.</p></div></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="meta">
        <span class="label ember">Phoenix I/O product · Healthcare transport</span>
        <h2>MedTransport</h2>
        <p>A dispatch, crew and fleet platform for non-emergency medical transport and ambulance companies. It covers patients and authorizations, trips and standing orders, a live dispatch board, crew credentials and vehicle inspections, and an Android crew app that keeps working offline and signs everything it syncs.</p>
        <p class="big"><i>8</i> phases in <i>11</i> days</p>
        <div class="kpis" aria-label="Project figures">
          <div><b>181</b><span>commits</span></div>
          <div><b>61</b><span>database migrations</span></div>
          <div><b>112</b><span>review findings, all fixed</span></div>
          <div><b>13</b><span>live-check scripts</span></div>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Secure sign-in and roles, company isolation enforced in both the app and the database, and a tamper-evident audit log with alerts</li>
          <li>Patients, payers, facilities, coverage and authorizations, with encrypted documents and CSV import and export</li>
          <li>Trips, standing orders, a dispatch board, maps, ETAs and live tracking</li>
          <li>Crew credentials and reminders, vehicle inspections, defects and capacity</li>
          <li>Kotlin crew app with a key vault, app lock, signatures and defect photos, plus signed offline sync with per-event locking and a review queue</li>
          <li>Every phase code-reviewed before the next began; security mapped to OWASP ASVS L2 for the web and MASVS L2 for the app</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="stackL" style="gap:20px;min-width:0">
        <div class="arch">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 440 250" role="img" aria-label="Architecture: Kotlin crew app with signed offline sync and a web dispatch board connect to the API, which enforces company isolation and stores data in PostgreSQL with a tamper-evident audit log.">
            <g class="n"><rect x="10" y="20" width="124" height="50" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="24" y="42">Crew app</text><text x="24" y="58">Kotlin · offline</text></g>
            <g class="n"><rect x="10" y="180" width="124" height="50" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="24" y="202">Dispatch board</text><text x="24" y="218">web · live map</text></g>
            <g class="n hot"><rect x="166" y="98" width="114" height="54" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="180" y="121">API</text><text x="180" y="138">roles · isolation</text></g>
            <g class="n"><rect x="310" y="40" width="124" height="50" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="322" y="62">PostgreSQL</text><text x="322" y="78">per-company rows</text></g>
            <g class="n"><rect x="310" y="160" width="124" height="50" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="322" y="182">Audit log</text><text x="322" y="198">tamper-evident</text></g>
            <path class="flow" d="M134 45 C 152 45, 150 115, 166 115"/><path class="flow" d="M134 205 C 152 205, 150 135, 166 135"/>
            <path d="M280 115 C 296 115, 296 65, 310 65"/><path d="M280 135 C 296 135, 296 185, 310 185"/>
            <text x="178" y="90">signed sync</text>
          </svg>
          <div class="cap"><span>Kotlin · PostgreSQL · web push</span><span>Applications · Regulated data · Cryptography</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="phasetrack" aria-label="Delivery phases">
          <div class="pt-head"><span class="label">Delivery phases</span><span class="label">8 of 12 done</span></div>
          <ol>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Sign-in, roles and audit</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Patients</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Trips and dispatch</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Crew and fleet</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Driver</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Android app</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Sync and review</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Crew confirms changes</span></li>
            <li class="now"><i></i><span>Shift and run</span></li>
            <li><i></i><span>Route monitoring</span></li>
            <li><i></i><span>Billing (837P / 835)</span></li>
            <li><i></i><span>ePCR (NEMSIS v3.5)</span></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="note">In active development and pre-production: go-live checks such as an outside penetration test are still open.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="meta">
        <span class="label ember">Phoenix I/O project · Financial services</span>
        <h2>High-frequency trading system</h2>
        <p>A proprietary trading firm needed one platform to trade across centralized exchanges and decentralized venues, fast enough to compete and secure enough to never expose a private key.</p>
        <p class="big"><i>&lt;1</i> ms · <i>$1B+</i> volume</p>
        <ul><li>Lock-free Go distributed system with a central sequencer across 2 blockchains and 19 venues</li><li>C++ high-frequency platform with FIX, WebSocket and REST connectivity</li><li>ECDSA and Ed25519 signing with zero key exposure</li><li>Automated reconciliation and AI-assisted log analysis with human review</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 440 250" role="img" aria-label="Architecture: exchange, blockchain venue and market data connectors feed a lock-free sequencer that drives strategies, a signer with zero key exposure, and reconciliation.">
          <g class="n"><rect x="10" y="14" width="110" height="44" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="24" y="34">Exchanges</text><text x="24" y="49">FIX · WebSocket</text></g>
          <g class="n"><rect x="10" y="103" width="110" height="44" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="24" y="123">19 venues</text><text x="24" y="138">2 blockchains</text></g>
          <g class="n"><rect x="10" y="192" width="110" height="44" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="24" y="212">Market data</text><text x="24" y="227">order books</text></g>
          <g class="n hot"><rect x="158" y="95" width="122" height="60" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="170" y="120">Sequencer</text><text x="170" y="137">lock-free · &lt;1 ms</text></g>
          <g class="n"><rect x="300" y="14" width="134" height="44" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="312" y="34">Strategies</text><text x="312" y="49">RFQ · routing</text></g>
          <g class="n"><rect x="300" y="103" width="134" height="44" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="312" y="123">Signer</text><text x="312" y="138">zero key exposure</text></g>
          <g class="n"><rect x="300" y="192" width="134" height="44" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="312" y="212">Reconciliation</text><text x="312" y="227">automated</text></g>
          <path class="flow" d="M120 36 C 140 36, 140 115, 158 115"/><path class="flow" d="M120 125 L158 125"/><path class="flow" d="M120 214 C 140 214, 140 135, 158 135"/>
          <path d="M280 115 C 290 115, 290 36, 300 36"/><path d="M280 125 L300 125"/><path d="M280 135 C 290 135, 290 214, 300 214"/>
        </svg>
        <div class="cap"><span>Go · C++ · FIX · EVM</span><span>Client name withheld</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
